    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2018-june/q4",
      "question": "<p>Part of the mains water system for a housing estate consists of water pipes buried beneath the ground surface. The water pipes are modelled as straight line segments. One water pipe, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span>, is buried beneath a particular road. With respect to a fixed origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>, the road surface is modelled as a plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x - 5y - 18z = 7\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span> passes through the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(-1, -1, -3)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(1, 2, -3)\"></span>. The units are in metres.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Use the model to calculate the acute angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span> and the road surface.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>A point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(-1, -2, 0)\"></span> lies on the road. A section of water pipe needs to be connected to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Using the model, find, to the nearest cm, the shortest length of pipe needed to connect <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
