    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2018-june/q5",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} -\\frac{1}{2} &amp; -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} &amp; -\\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Describe fully the single geometrical transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span> represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span>, represented by the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2 \\times 2\"></span> matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{B}\"></span>, is a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = -x\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Write down the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{B}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span> followed by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> is the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>, which is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{C}\"></span>,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{C}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) Show that there is a real number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1, k)\"></span> is invariant under <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
