      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2018-june/q6",
      "question": "<p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Use the standard results for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r\"></span> to show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} (3r - 2)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} n \\left[ 6n^2 - 3n - 1 \\right]\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Hence find any values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> for which</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=5}^{n} (3r - 2)^2 + 103 \\sum_{r=1}^{28} r \\cos \\left( \\frac{r\\pi}{2} \\right) = 3n^3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
