    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2018-june/q7",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(z) = z^3 + z^2 + pz + q\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>The equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(z) = 0\"></span> has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1, z_2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_3\"></span>.</p><p>When plotted on an Argand diagram, the points representing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1, z_2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_3\"></span> form the vertices of a triangle of area 35</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1 = 3\"></span>, find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></p>",
